  "body": "Found in the independent review of PR #401 (#317, carry the machined body into the next setup).\n\nWhat happens: #401's notes say the carry is refused when setups sit on different machines, but the program sim only checks the active setup's machine kind. No gouge path exists today, because posting mixed mounts is blocked at post time, but the sim's verdict across a machine change goes unrefused and the notes don't match the code.\nAlso: `stock_carry` / `setup_carry` only cover footprints that match. No test has an odd cell count plus a translation off the grid to pin that the carried grid's origin lines up with whole cells.\n\nDone means: the program sim refuses a carry between setups on different machines by name (a test pins the refusal text), and a test with an odd cell count and an off-grid translation pins carried-grid alignment.\n\nPart of #308.\n",
